ng and testing of advanced systems. It also provides a range of gas delivery solutions, such as precision thermal products, valves, connectors, industrial process connectors and valves, pneumatic actuators, manifolds and safety solutions, hoses, pressure gauges, gas lines, and component heaters, as well as complex weldments. In addition, the company offers assemblies, including gas and fluid delivery solutions, wafer transport systems, mechatronic assemblies, process modules, and sub-fab process equipment support racks; weldments and frames with exacting standards; heaters, sensors, and controllers for precise temperature control; integrated device manufacturers and OEMs validated process tool chamber parts cleaning and coating services; and tool part process optimization solutions, analytical verification of process tool chamber part cleaning effectiveness and micro contamination analysis of tool parts, wafers and depositions, chemicals, cleanroom materials, deionized water, and airborne molecular contamination. It primarily serves customers in the semiconductor capital equipment and semiconductor integrated device manufacturing industries, as well as display, consumer, medical, energy, industrial, and research equipment industries. The company was founded in 1991 and is headquartered in Hayward, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jinsong  Xiao | CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $990,976 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $296K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $2K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Ultra Clean Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $2.0B market cap on $2.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 16% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $15M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -14.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 203% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.0338158865823406},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $5.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-5338363.07},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 62/100): roic below cost of capital; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (UCTT) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_UCTT_Volatility_110426010601_1793772361.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793772361.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ultra Clean (UCTT) Upgraded to Buy: What Does It Mean for the Stock?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3020876/ultra-clean-uctt-upgraded-to-buy-what-does-it-mean-for-the-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3020876","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793635206.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a","analyst_action"]},{"title":"What UCTT's Q3 Beat and Strong Q4 Guidance Mean for Investors Now","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3020804/what-uctt-s-q3-beat-and-strong-q4-guidance-mean-for-investors-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog_plus%7Czer_report_insights-3020804","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793633940.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Is UCTT Worth Buying as Growth Accelerates but Cash Flow Wea